From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - accept an offset at the end of a scatterlist

aead_enqueue() looks up the start of the data with spu_sg_at_offset()
at req->assoclen. When the request has no data and src holds just the
associated data, as in an out-of-place GCM encryption of an empty
message with no associated data, that offset is the end of the list.
spu_sg_at_offset() then walks past the last entry and returns -EINVAL,
so the request fails:

  alg: aead: gcm-aes-iproc encryption failed on test vector 0;
  expected_error=0, actual_error=-22, cfg="out-of-place"

Return the last entry, with the offset at its end, when the distance
equals the length of the list. Callers then find no data there, and
spu_sg_count() counts no entries for it.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ int spu_sg_at_offset(struct scatterlist *sg, unsigned int skip,
 
 	next_index = sg->length;
 	while (next_index <= skip) {
+		if (next_index == skip && sg_is_last(sg))
+			break;
 		sg = sg_next(sg);
 		index = next_index;
 		if (!sg)
